  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat Version:\n\nBuild 1275\n\nDescription of the bug:\n\nWhen an object has a Rigidbody component with a Collider under the parent object the player gets launched across the world when they stand on it.\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n\nAdd the VRC Pickup script to an object and give that object a collider under the parent object for the player to stand on, standing or running across the object will launch the player. (repeatable on every object set up this way)\n\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\n\nHere is a Youtube video demonstrating the bug, first bed has the VRC Pickup script with Rigidbody component, second bed has only the Rigidbody component and the third bed has no scripts but the collider only. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b5FSXzs3BnQ\n\nAlso note the scripts and everything worked perfectly when testing inside of unity, only in VRchat client does this glitch occur.",
